{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789164466,"nonce":"VpVwSXx6WFxcHHU4/EUbcA4Dopw=","message":"Fixed in 297fa56 and 1766e81; verified in CI.\n\nNot an ash defect and not sqlite's. The conformance job built the wasm host and runtime object but never a side module, so on the wasm arms every sqlite primitive was unresolved and each of its tests threw -- eleven errors against a native arm at 1118/1118. Two steps were missing: build_wasm_hdll.py itself, then the rust-src component and a named clang-21 it turned out to need (the cached wasi sysroot is kept without wasi-sdk's own compiler).\n\nCI since: sys 1118/1118 with zero errors on interp, aot, wasm and wasm-fibers.","files":null}]}